.TH LAZYDECK 1 "2026-08-22" "lazydeck" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
lazydeck \- terminal UI and local API for Steam devkits
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B lazydeck
.br
.B lazydeck serve
.RI [ --fixture ]
.br
.B lazydeck version
.br
.B lazydeck help
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B lazydeck
is a terminal UI for pairing, inspecting, deploying to, and collecting logs
from Steam Deck and Steam Machine devkits. It uses the SteamOS devkit protocol
over the local network.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B lazydeck
Start the interactive terminal UI.
.TP
.B lazydeck serve
Start the local HTTP API used by the Godot and Unity editor integrations.
The server publishes its authenticated connection file at
.I $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/lazydeck/serve.json
on Linux.
.TP
.B lazydeck serve --fixture
Start the API using an in-memory backend. This is intended for integration
tests and does not connect to a Steam device.
.TP
.B lazydeck version
Print version and build metadata.
.TP
.B lazydeck help
Print command usage.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/lazydeck/devices.toml
Configured Steam devkits. Defaults to
.IR ~/.config/lazydeck/devices.toml .
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/lazydeck/config.yml
Optional custom TUI commands. Defaults to
.IR ~/.config/lazydeck/config.yml .
.TP
.I $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/lazydeck/serve.json
Authenticated connection information for editor integrations. This file is
created with mode 0600 and exists only for the desktop session.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B LAZYDECK_PYTHON_DIR
Override the bundled Python bridge location.
.TP
.B LAZYDECK_UV
Override the uv executable used to run the Python bridge.
.TP
.B LAZYDECK_SSH_STRICT
Set to 1 to reject changed Steam-devkit SSH host keys.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR systemctl (1),
.BR ssh (1),
.BR rsync (1)
.br
https://github.com/KevinTCoughlin/lazydeck
